# Naming Conventions

## Files

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Screen | `PascalCase.js` | `FamilyPlanOnboarding.js`, `LiveMeditationDoneDonate.js` |
| Component | `PascalCase.js` | `LiveMeditationDonateModal.js` |
| Reflux store | `{Domain}Store.js` or `{Domain}Controller.js` | `AppInfoStore.js`, `RNIapController.js` |
| Helper / logic | `PascalCase.js` or `camelCase.js` (match neighbors) | `Trackings.js`, `BranchHelper.js`, `communityForum.js` |
| Hook | `useXxx.js` | `useScreenInsets.js` |
| Style file | `camelCase.js` | `styleSheet.js`, `fontStyles.js` |
| Localization JSON | `<namespace>.json` per locale folder | `src/localization/en/miscellaneous.json` |

When extending a folder, **match the existing naming** in that folder rather than inventing a new convention.

## Symbols

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Component | `PascalCase` | `FamilyPlanOnboarding` |
| Function / variable | `camelCase` | `loadFamilyPlanProducts` |
| Constant (module-level, semantic) | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `FOO_LOADED`, `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT` |
| React state setter | `setCamelCase` | `setLoading` |
| Boolean | `is*`, `has*`, `can*`, `should*` prefix | `isLoading`, `hasMorePages` |
| Collection | plural noun | `tracks`, `journals` |
| Event constant | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` exported from store | `export const FOO_LOADED = 'FOO_LOADED'` |

## Avoid

- Single-letter variable names except for short loop indices (`i`, `j`).
- Hungarian-style prefixes (`strFoo`, `arrFoo`).
- Abbreviating beyond what's already common in the codebase (`btn`, `lbl`, `txt`). The repo uses `Button`, `Label`, `Text`.
- Re-using existing names with a slight twist (`User` vs `UserModel` vs `UserData`) — pick one and reuse it.

## File Placement Reminder

See `architecture.mdc` for which folder a new file belongs in. Naming alone doesn't fix being in the wrong place.
